#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105401 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7c9317eb-d1ce-5f42-b69b-a37e643b865b" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Vector Projection Using Angle and Magnitude"}] :question/id #uuid "3278333b-a29e-54c5-bc94-b5525bc6f751" :question/math-academy-id "e-14617" :question/problem "Suppose that $|\\,\\mathbf{a}\\,|=8,|\\,\\mathbf{b}\\,|=4$ and that the angle between the vectors is $\\theta = \\dfrac{5\\pi}{6}.$ Find the vector projection of $\\mathbf{a}$ onto $\\mathbf{b}$ in terms of the vector $\\mathbf{b}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the scalar projection as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{comp}}_{b}\\,a & =|\\,a\\,|\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =8\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{5\\pi }{6}) \\\\  & =8\\cdot (-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}) \\\\  & =-4\\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we find the unit vector that is parallel to $\\mathbf{b}\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{u} = \\dfrac{\\mathbf{b}}{|\\,\\mathbf{b}\\,|} = \\dfrac{\\mathbf{b}}{4} = \\dfrac{1}{4} \\mathbf{b}\n$$\n\nFinally, we compute the vector projection as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{b}\\,a & ={\\text{comp}}_{b}\\,a\\cdot u \\\\  & =-4\\sqrt{3}\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}b \\\\  & =-\\sqrt{3}b\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105402 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c0670172-77cb-5e88-b78d-e5136c06095f" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Vector Projection Using Components"}] :question/id #uuid "58b2269d-f998-5ba5-9df8-54ea422c43aa" :question/math-academy-id "e-14618" :question/problem "Let $\\mathbf{a}=\\langle 1,-3,5 \\rangle$ and $\\mathbf{b}=\\langle 5,-4,0 \\rangle$. Find the vector projection of $\\mathbf{a}$ onto $\\mathbf{b}$." :question/worked-solution "Using the formula for the vector projection, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{b}\\,a & =\\frac{a\\cdot b}{b\\cdot b}b \\\\  & =\\frac{{a}_{x}{b}_{x}+{a}_{y}{b}_{y}+{a}_{z}{b}_{z}}{{b}_{x}^{2}+{b}_{y}^{2}+{b}_{z}^{2}}b \\\\  & =\\frac{1\\cdot 5+(-3)\\cdot (-4)+5\\cdot 0}{{5}^{2}+(-4)^{2}+{0}^{2}}b \\\\  & =\\frac{17}{41}⟨5,-4,0⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{85}{41},-\\frac{68}{41},0⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105403 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "84c96375-27d5-5ada-a952-34e09b3e92bf" :knowledge-point/title "Perpendicular Vectors"}] :question/id #uuid "663f3f5e-56cf-5517-ba1e-d1a355767e0b" :question/math-academy-id "e-14619" :question/problem "Let $[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$ and $[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]$. Find the vector projection of $\\mathbf{a}$ onto $\\mathbf{b}$." :question/worked-solution "Using the formula for the vector projection, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{b}\\,a & =\\frac{a\\cdot b}{b\\cdot b}b \\\\  & =\\frac{{a}_{x}{b}_{x}+{a}_{y}{b}_{y}+{a}_{z}{b}_{z}}{{b}_{x}^{2}+{b}_{y}^{2}+{b}_{z}^{2}}b \\\\  & =\\frac{1\\cdot 1+0\\cdot 5+1\\cdot (-1)}{{1}^{2}+{5}^{2}+(-1)^{2}}b \\\\  & =\\frac{0}{{1}^{2}+{5}^{2}+(-1)^{2}}b \\\\  & =⟨0,0,0⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278131 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c0670172-77cb-5e88-b78d-e5136c06095f" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Vector Projection Using Components"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7ac89813-eaca-5387-a2b6-0d02fd8454ba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\sqrt{2},\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2},1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278133} {:answer/id #uuid "0e59a8e3-387e-5f83-bec5-0d38f4ae21f8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨0,0,0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278134} {:answer/id #uuid "4ef1b113-fe6c-519b-8127-c191b645f492" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨3\\sqrt{2},\\frac{3\\sqrt{2}}{2},3⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278135} {:answer/id #uuid "4aed13cc-9ab2-52d0-8d21-3832ca7e15de" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨6,3,3\\sqrt{2}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278136} {:answer/id #uuid "9bde2a5f-5a7c-55ac-8713-2718f5108164" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2,1,\\sqrt{2}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278137}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9bde2a5f-5a7c-55ac-8713-2718f5108164" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2,1,\\sqrt{2}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278137} :answer-field/id #uuid "e2aef5f8-4e90-57ed-878d-b61826033a23" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278132}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "07d400bc-8e75-529a-86cf-3fbedf09676f" :question/math-academy-id "q-126507" :question/problem "Let $a=[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 3\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}]$ and $b=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].$ Find the vector projection of $b$ onto $a.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the formula for the vector projection, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{a}\\,b & =\\frac{a\\cdot b}{a\\cdot a}a \\\\  & =\\frac{{a}_{x}{b}_{x}+{a}_{y}{b}_{y}+{a}_{z}{b}_{z}}{{a}_{x}^{2}+{a}_{y}^{2}+{a}_{z}^{2}}a \\\\  & =\\frac{6\\cdot 3+3\\cdot 1+3\\sqrt{2}\\cdot 0}{{6}^{2}+{3}^{2}+(3\\sqrt{2})^{2}}a \\\\  & =\\frac{21}{63}⟨6,3,3\\sqrt{2}⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}⟨6,3,3\\sqrt{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2,1,\\sqrt{2}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278138 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c0670172-77cb-5e88-b78d-e5136c06095f" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Vector Projection Using Components"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bb5b189a-a239-5470-8788-4faacd32cb38" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨3\\sqrt{2},3,0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278140} {:answer/id #uuid "1433dd63-e106-5e2a-a9b0-9d596b00d07f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨0,0,0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278141} {:answer/id #uuid "b7c2e29b-7068-557b-8cc7-55acec4330b1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-\\sqrt{2},-1,0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278142} {:answer/id #uuid "a0b259a5-5948-5fc3-a399-efeadb1bb56f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨0,-\\frac{9}{4},-\\frac{3}{4}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278143} {:answer/id #uuid "bc3df04f-5c06-5456-a867-4e13c336b9aa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-\\sqrt{2},1,0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278144}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b7c2e29b-7068-557b-8cc7-55acec4330b1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-\\sqrt{2},-1,0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278142} :answer-field/id #uuid "3d280dbb-b209-5df3-8069-73c3ea8485e2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278139}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b8e013a5-b3de-5807-ade4-01f7026dfed4" :question/math-academy-id "q-18377" :question/problem "Let $a=⟨0,-3,1⟩$ and $b=⟨\\sqrt{2},1,0⟩.$ Find the vector projection of $a$ onto $b.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the formula for the vector projection, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{b}\\,a & =\\frac{a\\cdot b}{b\\cdot b}b \\\\  & =\\frac{{a}_{x}{b}_{x}+{a}_{y}{b}_{y}+{a}_{z}{b}_{z}}{{b}_{x}^{2}+{b}_{y}^{2}+{b}_{z}^{2}}b \\\\  & =\\frac{0\\cdot \\sqrt{2}+(-3)\\cdot 1+1\\cdot 0}{(\\sqrt{2})^{2}+{1}^{2}+{0}^{2}}b \\\\  & =\\frac{-3}{3}⟨\\sqrt{2},1,0⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\sqrt{2},-1,0⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278145 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c0670172-77cb-5e88-b78d-e5136c06095f" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Vector Projection Using Components"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "400bd356-c1fe-5ed0-8242-025adf5f7a15" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨0,0,0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278147} {:answer/id #uuid "7cb0afd9-989d-53b8-86c0-53eb4639a4c1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-\\frac{57}{35},\\frac{19}{14},-\\frac{57}{35}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278148} {:answer/id #uuid "ca29111c-2e32-53d7-8c62-ce1b88a8033e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-\\frac{57}{35},\\frac{19}{14},-\\frac{57}{70}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278149} {:answer/id #uuid "0ac030f5-2ec3-5198-9d0d-fcd67017c94c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-\\frac{57}{35},\\frac{19}{35},-\\frac{57}{35}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278150} {:answer/id #uuid "c87db22e-acff-5a20-a106-6fc38ab20a59" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-\\frac{57}{70},\\frac{19}{14},-\\frac{57}{70}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278151}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ca29111c-2e32-53d7-8c62-ce1b88a8033e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-\\frac{57}{35},\\frac{19}{14},-\\frac{57}{70}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278149} :answer-field/id #uuid "d5784fa7-b9b4-503f-8178-7f044d1f4788" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278146}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "16afdc3e-3de7-5f89-a577-96cb66b16553" :question/math-academy-id "q-19194" :question/problem "Let $a=⟨-2,-1,-4⟩$ and $b=⟨6,-5,3⟩.$ Find the vector projection of $a$ onto $b.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the formula for the vector projection, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{b}\\,a & =\\frac{a\\cdot b}{b\\cdot b}b \\\\  & =\\frac{{a}_{x}{b}_{x}+{a}_{y}{b}_{y}+{a}_{z}{b}_{z}}{{b}_{x}^{2}+{b}_{y}^{2}+{b}_{z}^{2}}b \\\\  & =\\frac{(-2)\\cdot 6+(-1)\\cdot (-5)+(-4)\\cdot 3}{{6}^{2}+(-5)^{2}+{3}^{2}}b \\\\  & =-\\frac{19}{70}⟨6,-5,3⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\frac{57}{35},\\frac{19}{14},-\\frac{57}{70}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278152 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7c9317eb-d1ce-5f42-b69b-a37e643b865b" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Vector Projection Using Angle and Magnitude"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "172c5ba2-541e-5ce0-8c73-13f6018d1640" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6\\sqrt{2}b" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278154} {:answer/id #uuid "a1303fc3-54c1-5760-9384-5e0c7e0cba79" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-9\\sqrt{2}b" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278155} {:answer/id #uuid "ab256ca4-7de4-52c8-ace1-038bf415592a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3\\sqrt{2}b" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278156} {:answer/id #uuid "ace4ed9e-74f8-5e7d-8df6-9aa90cbf332b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-18\\sqrt{2}b" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278157} {:answer/id #uuid "de3d366f-8710-51b2-a061-da2b87f521e0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-12\\sqrt{2}b" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278158}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ab256ca4-7de4-52c8-ace1-038bf415592a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3\\sqrt{2}b" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278156} :answer-field/id #uuid "0215dfd6-da55-5f6a-91b5-8fa0a78fd7b0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278153}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6fb2408a-be21-5e6c-bc42-4b7ac101fd5c" :question/math-academy-id "q-19220" :question/problem "Suppose that $|\\,a\\,|=36$, $|\\,b\\,|=6$ and that the angle between the vectors is $\\theta ={135}^{∘}.$ Find the vector projection of $a$ onto $b$ in terms of the vector $b.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the scalar projection as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{comp}}_{b}\\,a & =|\\,a\\,|\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =36\\operatorname{cos}⁡({135}^{∘}) \\\\  & =36\\cdot (-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}) \\\\  & =-18\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we find the unit vector that is parallel to $b:$\n\n$$\nu=\\frac{b}{|\\,b\\,|}=\\frac{b}{6}=\\frac{1}{6}b\n$$\n\nFinally, we compute the vector projection as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{b}\\,a & ={\\text{comp}}_{b}\\,a\\cdot u \\\\  & =(-18\\sqrt{2})\\cdot \\frac{1}{6}b \\\\  & =-3\\sqrt{2}b\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278159 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "84c96375-27d5-5ada-a952-34e09b3e92bf" :knowledge-point/title "Perpendicular Vectors"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "79391234-73d9-5ee0-92b9-8f5990d9c344" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278161} {:answer/id #uuid "8723e7a4-352c-5419-b117-c1cf379034f4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278162} {:answer/id #uuid "b24546f6-e090-5171-a69e-f59055facd6e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278163} {:answer/id #uuid "89beb507-2355-56db-ad70-2ff06beda27d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278164} {:answer/id #uuid "1d7418e3-574b-55d3-8644-e430728584e7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278165}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "89beb507-2355-56db-ad70-2ff06beda27d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278164} :answer-field/id #uuid "3d982e5d-4c5a-5a80-8ae6-7e8e38a04701" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278160}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "5b48b4f7-6f79-595f-aadb-f1b18c1eb86c" :question/math-academy-id "q-212458" :question/problem "Let $a=⟨-5,-3,1⟩$ and $b=⟨x,-2,-3⟩.$ Given that the projection of $a$ onto $b$ is the zero vector, find the value of $x.$" :question/worked-solution "Since $a$ is a nonzero vector, its projection onto another nonzero vector $b$ equals the zero vector only when the vectors are perpendicular. \n\nSo, we must have\n\n$$\na⊥b\\,⟹\\,a\\cdot b=0.\n$$\n\nComputing the dot product, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot b & ={a}_{x}\\cdot {b}_{x}+{a}_{y}\\cdot {b}_{y}+{a}_{z}\\cdot {b}_{z} \\\\  & =-5\\cdot x+(-3)\\cdot (-2)+1\\cdot (-3) \\\\  & =3-5x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting the dot product equal to $0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot b & =0 \\\\ 3-5x & =0 \\\\ -5x & =-3 \\\\ x & =\\frac{3}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278166 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7c9317eb-d1ce-5f42-b69b-a37e643b865b" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Vector Projection Using Angle and Magnitude"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e26dee69-5eff-5f6d-872c-2baab6a6ddf2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278168} {:answer/id #uuid "2dcc5c85-5907-532e-9db5-89520567f8fd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278169}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2dcc5c85-5907-532e-9db5-89520567f8fd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278169} :answer-field/id #uuid "9ea6baab-a0e4-5a9c-b45f-3c6cc5a86359" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278167}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "637cb119-eb86-568a-a2d9-f23e98e4459a" :question/math-academy-id "q-275228" :question/problem "Suppose that $|\\,p\\,|=6$, $|\\,q\\,|=12$ and that the angle between the vectors is $\\theta ={150}^{∘}.$ Find the vector projection of $q$ onto $p$ in terms of the vector $p.$\n\n${\\text{proj}}_{p}\\,q=$\n{{field-1}}\n$p$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the scalar projection as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{comp}}_{p}\\,q & =|\\,q\\,|\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =12\\operatorname{cos}⁡({150}^{∘}) \\\\  & =12\\cdot (-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}) \\\\  & =-6\\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we find the unit vector that is parallel to $p:$\n\n$$\nu=\\frac{p}{|\\,p\\,|}=\\frac{p}{6}=\\frac{1}{6}p\n$$\n\nFinally, we compute the vector projection as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{p}\\,q & ={\\text{comp}}_{p}\\,q\\cdot u \\\\  & =-6\\sqrt{3}\\cdot \\frac{1}{6}p \\\\  & =-\\sqrt{3}\\,p\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278170 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c0670172-77cb-5e88-b78d-e5136c06095f" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Vector Projection Using Components"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e15fe54c-65a3-5c95-bde0-75492747c438" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278172} {:answer/id #uuid "7541c8ad-38ab-5c2f-ac90-24aa4e64367b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278173}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7541c8ad-38ab-5c2f-ac90-24aa4e64367b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278173} :answer-field/id #uuid "12f32dd3-ed56-5374-8c14-6d495b8663ea" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278171} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "619599e1-e9bd-5cbd-bc65-bf0146fc09c0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{7}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278175}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "619599e1-e9bd-5cbd-bc65-bf0146fc09c0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{7}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278175} :answer-field/id #uuid "1b650bda-a627-56ef-bab2-a99e8db80137" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278174} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4fd3150e-167c-53cf-939d-b549cc2303e2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{35}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278177}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4fd3150e-167c-53cf-939d-b549cc2303e2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{35}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278177} :answer-field/id #uuid "b9892346-cf69-5ae3-b300-41cbbc14982e" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278176}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "af7b2065-ddd7-541d-b600-09c9bbc528d5" :question/math-academy-id "q-275230" :question/problem "Let $c=⟨2,-1,6⟩$ and $d=⟨4,-2,10⟩.$ Find the vector projection of $c$ onto $d.$\n\n${\\text{proj}}_{d}\\,c=⟨$\n{{field-1}}$,$\n{{field-2}}$,$\n{{field-3}}\n$⟩$" :question/worked-solution "Using the formula for the vector projection, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{d}\\,c & =\\frac{c\\cdot d}{d\\cdot d}d \\\\  & =\\frac{{c}_{x}{d}_{x}+{c}_{y}{d}_{y}+{c}_{z}{d}_{z}}{{d}_{x}^{2}+{d}_{y}^{2}+{d}_{z}^{2}}d \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\cdot 4+(-1)\\cdot (-2)+6\\cdot 10}{{4}^{2}+(-2)^{2}+{10}^{2}}d \\\\  & =\\frac{70}{120}⟨4,-2,10⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{12}⟨4,-2,10⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\,\\frac{7}{3},-\\frac{7}{6},\\frac{35}{6}\\,⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278178 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c0670172-77cb-5e88-b78d-e5136c06095f" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Vector Projection Using Components"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "866c8a7b-de71-53a7-97c2-ea76f926d63a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278180}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "866c8a7b-de71-53a7-97c2-ea76f926d63a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278180} :answer-field/id #uuid "9ebf82e7-74bf-5b36-a133-53530e5f87ba" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278179} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c7ff6b03-a262-55a4-a420-0feba36b1171" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278182}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c7ff6b03-a262-55a4-a420-0feba36b1171" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278182} :answer-field/id #uuid "318a4456-9027-551b-992d-5940b9d19f50" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278181} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f314b0e7-1685-58df-952e-e83e1e66fa55" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278184}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f314b0e7-1685-58df-952e-e83e1e66fa55" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278184} :answer-field/id #uuid "d761b493-fcf8-5740-b480-55099ddae3a9" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278183}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ecf868e0-e21c-5ab5-a72f-7aca1872c9a6" :question/math-academy-id "q-275231" :question/problem "Let $c=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 8 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]$ and $d=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}].$ Find the vector projection of $c$ onto $d.$\n\n${\\text{proj}}_{d}\\,c=⟨$  \n\n{{field-1}},\n\n{{field-2}},\n\n{{field-3}}\n\n$⟩$" :question/worked-solution "Using the formula for the vector projection, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{d}\\,c & =\\frac{c\\cdot d}{d\\cdot d}d \\\\  & =\\frac{{c}_{x}{d}_{x}+{c}_{y}{d}_{y}+{c}_{z}{d}_{z}}{{d}_{x}^{2}+{d}_{y}^{2}+{d}_{z}^{2}}d \\\\  & =\\frac{(-2)\\cdot (-1)+8\\cdot 3+(-1)\\cdot (-2)}{(-1)^{2}+{3}^{2}+(-2)^{2}}d \\\\  & =\\frac{28}{14}⟨-1,3,-2⟩ \\\\  & =2⟨-1,3,-2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-2,6,-4⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278185 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "84c96375-27d5-5ada-a952-34e09b3e92bf" :knowledge-point/title "Perpendicular Vectors"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "820db87f-2659-51f7-828b-46a83f5bec34" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278187}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "820db87f-2659-51f7-828b-46a83f5bec34" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278187} :answer-field/id #uuid "b0dfc3fb-73ec-54eb-8092-aff33d72e5c5" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278186} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "247064a8-06cc-52b3-8c5a-4d8ca8915dad" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278189}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "247064a8-06cc-52b3-8c5a-4d8ca8915dad" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278189} :answer-field/id #uuid "a5cd5646-c658-5b94-be49-28619795bf55" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278188} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b018a20e-977a-5740-9d85-b9b40abc5a7d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278191}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b018a20e-977a-5740-9d85-b9b40abc5a7d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278191} :answer-field/id #uuid "e8b28e03-aa37-5376-b773-e929015e3759" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278190}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "737e0d38-fcff-5bfe-9948-3a9d47dce708" :question/math-academy-id "q-275235" :question/problem "Let $c=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$ and $d=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].$ Find the vector projection of $c$ onto $d.$\n\n${\\text{proj}}_{d}\\,c=⟨$\n\n{{field-1}},\n\n{{field-2}},\n\n{{field-3}}\n\n$⟩$" :question/worked-solution "Using the formula for the vector projection, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{d}\\,c & =\\frac{c\\cdot d}{d\\cdot d}d \\\\  & =\\frac{{c}_{x}{d}_{x}+{c}_{y}{d}_{y}+{c}_{z}{d}_{z}}{{d}_{x}^{2}+{d}_{y}^{2}+{d}_{z}^{2}}d \\\\  & =\\frac{(-2)\\cdot 2+0\\cdot 3+1\\cdot 4}{{2}^{2}+{3}^{2}+{4}^{2}}d \\\\  & =\\frac{0}{29}d \\\\  & =⟨0,0,0⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278192 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "84c96375-27d5-5ada-a952-34e09b3e92bf" :knowledge-point/title "Perpendicular Vectors"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3d6cefe9-ad1a-5c96-89ee-13765cab6bdc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278194} {:answer/id #uuid "b2f9ca16-7042-569a-baeb-d1ce8d29aa01" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278195}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3d6cefe9-ad1a-5c96-89ee-13765cab6bdc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278194} :answer-field/id #uuid "8e7fdc11-8a2f-532b-9337-bd8dcc7ccf8f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278193}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ba2dc2b6-282e-5a04-8a40-e8efff6fe0f3" :question/math-academy-id "q-275237" :question/problem "Let $a=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]$ and $b=[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ 3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$ Given that the projection of $a$ onto $b$ is the zero vector, find the value of $x.$\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Since $a$ is a nonzero vector, its projection onto another nonzero vector $b$ equals the zero vector only when the vectors are perpendicular. \n\nSo, we must have\n\n$$\na⊥b\\,⟹\\,a\\cdot b=0.\n$$\n\nComputing the dot product, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot b & ={a}_{x}\\cdot {b}_{x}+{a}_{y}\\cdot {b}_{y}+{a}_{z}\\cdot {b}_{z} \\\\  & =-2\\cdot x+1\\cdot 3+2\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =-2x+5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting the dot product equal to $0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot b & =0 \\\\ -2x+5 & =0 \\\\ 2x & =5 \\\\ x & =\\frac{5}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278196 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7c9317eb-d1ce-5f42-b69b-a37e643b865b" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Vector Projection Using Angle and Magnitude"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d20b519a-bd74-56f6-ab0d-28c760680985" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278198}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d20b519a-bd74-56f6-ab0d-28c760680985" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278198} :answer-field/id #uuid "bcc5df4b-5be8-53c5-ae41-8c913d42951b" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278197}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b32d4bc6-b577-5cf1-a1b8-28f5d0c75f21" :question/math-academy-id "q-316441" :question/problem "Suppose that $|\\,a\\,|=4$, $|\\,b\\,|=8\\sqrt{2}$ and that the angle between the vectors is $\\theta =\\frac{\\pi }{4}.$ Find the vector projection of $b$ onto $a$ in terms of the vector $a.$\n\n${\\text{proj}}_{a}\\,b=$\n{{field-1}}\n$a$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the scalar projection as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{comp}}_{a}\\,b & =|\\,b\\,|\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =8\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4}) \\\\  & =8\\sqrt{2}\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\\\  & =8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we find the unit vector that is parallel to $a:$\n\n$$\nu=\\frac{a}{|\\,a\\,|}=\\frac{a}{4}=\\frac{1}{4}a\n$$\n\nFinally, we compute the vector projection as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{a}\\,b & ={\\text{comp}}_{a}\\,b\\cdot u \\\\  & =8\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}a \\\\  & =2\\,a\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278199 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "84c96375-27d5-5ada-a952-34e09b3e92bf" :knowledge-point/title "Perpendicular Vectors"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "69eee15f-675e-5451-9bf0-87f26f881a43" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278201}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "69eee15f-675e-5451-9bf0-87f26f881a43" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278201} :answer-field/id #uuid "6889c208-b26b-546c-9fe1-cb0a3c998435" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278200}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "6fd1a3fd-cf3d-56c3-88b8-eb3ea7bb8999" :question/math-academy-id "q-316761" :question/problem "Let $r=⟨-5,1,3⟩$ and $s=⟨n,-2,4⟩.$ Given that the projection of $r$ onto $s$ is the zero vector, find the value of $n.$\n\n$n=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Since $r$ is a nonzero vector, its projection onto another nonzero vector $s$ equals the zero vector only when the vectors are perpendicular. \n\nSo, we must have\n\n$$\nr⊥s\\,⟹\\,r\\cdot s=0.\n$$\n\nComputing the dot product, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot s & ={r}_{x}\\cdot {s}_{x}+{r}_{y}\\cdot {s}_{y}+{r}_{z}\\cdot {s}_{z} \\\\  & =(-5)\\cdot n+1\\cdot (-2)+3\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =-5n-2+12 \\\\  & =10-5n.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting the dot product equal to $0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot s & =0 \\\\ 10-5n & =0 \\\\ n & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278202 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "84c96375-27d5-5ada-a952-34e09b3e92bf" :knowledge-point/title "Perpendicular Vectors"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "82a70726-08cf-54f3-82ae-93b3c5321b0f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278204} {:answer/id #uuid "f560ffaa-3949-53fe-847f-ae73129b4267" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278205}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f560ffaa-3949-53fe-847f-ae73129b4267" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278205} :answer-field/id #uuid "4ad32d67-6aa1-57f8-aa69-21ef2b0f0245" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278203} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "25dc21fb-21d2-5000-9cdd-a04443408ce8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278207}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "25dc21fb-21d2-5000-9cdd-a04443408ce8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278207} :answer-field/id #uuid "48d4ad65-36d5-5cd5-a889-74de85618f2f" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278206} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5ea563aa-b2ad-5c02-b280-00bcc3d1ebe5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278209}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5ea563aa-b2ad-5c02-b280-00bcc3d1ebe5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278209} :answer-field/id #uuid "92d93412-b3d5-5edf-8064-584c952a5609" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278208}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d76899f3-011a-5326-9aaa-6e8e8b6af9c0" :question/math-academy-id "q-317924" :question/problem "Let $u=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$ and $v=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].$ Find the vector projection of $u$ onto $v.$\n\n${\\text{proj}}_{v}\\,u=⟨$\n{{field-1}}$,$\n{{field-2}}$,$\n{{field-3}}\n$⟩$" :question/worked-solution "Using the formula for the vector projection, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{v}\\,u & =\\frac{u\\cdot v}{v\\cdot v}v \\\\  & =\\frac{{u}_{x}{v}_{x}+{u}_{y}{v}_{y}+{u}_{z}{v}_{z}}{{v}_{x}^{2}+{v}_{y}^{2}+{v}_{z}^{2}}v \\\\  & =\\frac{(1)\\cdot 2+(-2)\\cdot 1+(1)\\cdot 0}{{2}^{2}+{1}^{2}+{0}^{2}}v \\\\  & =\\frac{0}{5}v \\\\  & =⟨\\,0,0,0\\,⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278210 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7c9317eb-d1ce-5f42-b69b-a37e643b865b" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Vector Projection Using Angle and Magnitude"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cfe6c786-5f7b-5f3d-b8dc-f349abe412be" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}q" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278212} {:answer/id #uuid "e7ce84f3-93b6-573e-b678-4a97c0c0a224" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}q" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278213} {:answer/id #uuid "1c1adcba-4888-5a1c-b1c2-7e2b2caa70de" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{2}q" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278214} {:answer/id #uuid "aa8c838b-e8a3-52f5-a161-6036f6081877" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}q" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278215} {:answer/id #uuid "55efa673-a429-573b-b27f-94871ed5cb30" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2q" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278216}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "aa8c838b-e8a3-52f5-a161-6036f6081877" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}q" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278215} :answer-field/id #uuid "5a3f24eb-b742-501d-86fd-75674074b370" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278211}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "47f66d89-dd00-524e-9906-ac4f9a9f0e84" :question/math-academy-id "q-71835" :question/problem "Suppose that $|\\,p\\,|=8$, $|\\,q\\,|=4$ and that the angle between the vectors is $\\theta =\\frac{\\pi }{4}.$ Find the vector projection of $p$ onto $q$ in terms of the vector $q.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the scalar projection as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{comp}}_{q}\\,p & =|\\,p\\,|\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =8\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4}) \\\\  & =8\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\\\  & =4\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we find the unit vector that is parallel to $q:$\n\n$$\nu=\\frac{q}{|\\,q\\,|}=\\frac{q}{4}=\\frac{1}{4}q\n$$\n\nFinally, we compute the vector projection as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{b}\\,p & ={\\text{comp}}_{q}\\,p\\cdot u \\\\  & =4\\sqrt{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}q \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}q\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278217 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7c9317eb-d1ce-5f42-b69b-a37e643b865b" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Vector Projection Using Angle and Magnitude"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ece23503-bd50-5b21-94c0-5a21dd3f5a7e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{5}d" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278219} {:answer/id #uuid "b2f3bbbd-559f-5e27-9190-64dc733578f7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5d" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278220} {:answer/id #uuid "01bacc67-0858-554d-a2ad-adfed5f8dc32" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}d" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278221} {:answer/id #uuid "f6da54aa-6722-520c-8d57-601765094e27" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2\\sqrt{3}}{5}d" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278222} {:answer/id #uuid "1d7ffe4d-4b39-59ef-b4ff-61a6dce957f7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5\\sqrt{3}}{3}d" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278223}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "01bacc67-0858-554d-a2ad-adfed5f8dc32" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}d" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278221} :answer-field/id #uuid "5c9ee979-e0da-5150-9eaf-e21e2bc6decb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278218}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "7ba84402-0df7-51f8-9c09-70d13a0fe926" :question/math-academy-id "q-71838" :question/problem "Suppose that $|\\,c\\,|=10$, $|\\,d\\,|=2\\sqrt{3}$ and that the angle between the vectors is $\\theta ={30}^{∘}.$ Find the vector projection of $c$ onto $d$ in terms of the vector $d.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the scalar projection as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{comp}}_{d}\\,c & =|\\,c\\,|\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =10\\operatorname{cos}⁡({30}^{∘}) \\\\  & =10\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} \\\\  & =5\\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we find the unit vector that is parallel to $d:$\n\n$$\nu=\\frac{d}{|\\,d\\,|}=\\frac{d}{2\\sqrt{3}}=\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{3}}d\n$$\n\nFinally, we compute the vector projection as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{d}\\,c & ={\\text{comp}}_{d}\\,c\\cdot u \\\\  & =5\\sqrt{3}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{3}}d \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}d\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
